  "generated_text": "To solve the problem, we need to evaluate the expression $\\frac{x^6-16x^3+64}{x^3-8}$ when $x=6$.\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=6$ into the expression:\n$$\\frac{6^6-16(6^3)+64}{6^3-8}$$\n\nNext, we simplify the numerator and denominator separately:\n$$\\frac{6^6-16(6^3)+64}{6^3-8} = \\frac{46656-16(216)+64}{216-8}$$\n$$= \\frac{46656-3456+64}{208}$$\n$$= \\frac{43264}{208}$$\n\nNow, we simplify the fraction:\n$$\\frac{43264}{208} = \\frac{10816}{52}$$\n$$= \\frac{2704}{13}$$\n$$= \\boxed{208}$$\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{208}.",
